Known Bugs

LAN adapter not detected during OOBE (Offline & September 2026 versions)

What happens: If you already have a LAN adapter plugged in before reaching OOBE, Windows 11's OOBE fails to detect it — it behaves as if there's no internet connection at all. (Yes, I'm blaming Microsoft for this one.)

How to fix it: Unplug the LAN cable from the adapter, or unplug the adapter itself from the USB port/hub, then plug it back in. I use laptops, so I've tested this with both USB 2.0 and USB 3.0 TP-Link USB-to-LAN adapters.

Why this works: My best guess is that this resets the network interface, forcing the buggy OOBE (Windows installer) to re-scan for the LAN adapter. Once it detects it, the connection indicator will spin while it grabs an IP address, and you'll be connected to the internet shortly after.

A note on support: I'm a single dev with limited time, so if you run into new bugs, please leave a comment and I'll do my best to help figure it out.
